Eliminating x from first two equations gives 7y + 8z = 1, and subtracting first from third gives y + (a - 6)z = b - 4
For infinitely many solutions these two equations in y and z coincide, so a - 6 = \frac{8}{7} and b - 4 = \frac{1}{7}, giving b = \frac{29}{7}
Then a - b = \frac{50}{7} - \frac{29}{7} = 3, so (a, b) lies on x - y = 3 matches option B → (B)

